{
 "_doc": "Data the brainstorm home page draws from. It mirrors docs/00-OVERVIEW.md (which is canon — if they disagree, the doc wins and this file is stale). Classes: [id, name, primary role, mechanic, hybrid role, build, resource]. Kept as JSON so the home page has no hard-coded content.",
 "title": "Wildmarch",
 "tagline": "Everyone starts with a stick and one spell. The Wildmarch decides the rest.",
 "pitch": "An online action RPG with a shared, MMO-style world on one continent, built for groups of up to five. You start in a farming valley with one spell and leave on foot. Every region north is harder, and most of what makes a character feel powerful — the dodge roll, the mount, your class's signature trick, talents, travel routes, deeper dungeons — unlocks as you level or finish an important quest. A sibling of Farhold: same Chibi 2 characters, items, perks, voices and combat feel, without the planet sandbox — plus other players, thirty bespoke (often hybrid) class kits and boss fights you learn.",
 "pillars": [
  [
   "Unlock as you go",
   "A new character is simple on purpose; features arrive as you level or finish key quests."
  ],
  [
   "Thirty classes, thirty kits",
   "No two classes share a spell. Most can fill a second role — a mage can tank, a pyromancer can heal."
  ],
  [
   "Readable danger",
   "Every attack that can kill you is telegraphed before it lands."
  ],
  [
   "Bosses are the normal game",
   "Void zones, soaks, safe zones and talking bosses in the open world and in five-player dungeons."
  ],
  [
   "Loot worth talking about",
   "Sockets, jewels, souls, tags, special rarities, class sets and legendaries that change play."
  ],
  [
   "Together or alone",
   "The open world and Normal dungeons can be done solo with followers."
  ]
 ],
